rlottetown)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/St._Peter%27s_Cathedral_Charlottetown.jpg/960px-St._Peter%27s_Cathedral_Charlottetown.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Jean Canfield Building","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":46.237,"lo":-63.1299,"d":766,"ds":"The Jean Canfield Building is a Government of Canada office building located in Charlottetown, Prince Edward Island. It is named after Jean Canfield, the first woman elected to the Legislative Assembly of Prince Edward Island. The Jean Canfield building is one of the most environmentally friendly buildings ever constructed by Public Works and Government Services Canada.","wpu":"Jean Canfield Building","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Jean_Canfield_Building_2.jpg/960px-Jean_Canfield_Building_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Victoria Park, Charlottetown","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":46.229722,"lo":-63.14,"d":1162,"ds":"Victoria Park is a waterfront park in the city of Charlottetown, Prince Edward Island, Canada.","wpu":"Victoria Park, Charlottetown","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Aug06-vol4_176_%28223824904%29.jpg/960px-Aug06-vol4_176_%28223824904%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Hillsborough River Bridge","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":46.236083,"lo":-63.104611,"d":1666,"ds":"The Hillsborough River Bridge is a bridge crossing the Hillsborough River estuary between Charlottetown and Stratford in Queens County, Prince Edward Island. The current road bridge, built in 1962, replaced a 1905 rail bridge crossing the same span which was known by the same name. The first bridge was built by the Prince Edward Island Railway to complete a rail line from Charlottetown to Murray River.","wpu":"Hillsborough River Bridge","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/2021_Hillsborough_River_Bridge_01.jpg/960px-2021_Hillsborough_River_Bridge_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Ardgowan, Prince Edward Island","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":46.251981,"lo":-63.126283,"d":2335,"ds":"Ardgowan is a National Historic Site of Canada located in Parkdale, Prince Edward Island, currently a neighbourhood of the city of Charlottetown. The Ardgowan estate contains the country cottage of William Henry Pope, one of the Fathers of Confederation.","wpu":"Ardgowan, Prince Edward Island","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Ardgowan%2C_Prince_Edward_Island.jpg/960px-Ardgowan%2C_Prince_Edward_Island.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Stratford, Prince Edward Island","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":46.216664,"lo":-63.089331,"d":3173,"ds":"Stratford is a town located in Queens County, Prince Edward Island, Canada. Situated immediately southeast of the city of Charlottetown, Stratford recorded a population of 10,927 in the 2021 census. The town is the third-largest municipality in the province and has experienced population growth in recent decades since improvements were made to the Hillsborough River Bridge connecting the town with Charlottetown.","wpu":"Stratford, Prince Edward Island","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Stratford%2C_Prince_Edward_Island%2C_Canada.jpg/960px-Stratford%2C_Prince_Edward_Island%2C_Canada.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"York Point, Prince Edward Island","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":46.214278,"lo":-63.163694,"d":3509,"ds":"York Point is an unincorporated Canadian community in Queens County, Prince Edward Island. In 1996 it was amalgamated into the town of Cornwall. The community is centred on the York Point Road, which runs to North Point, a point of land formed by tidal inlets of the North (Yorke) River and the West (Elliot) River on the western side of Charlottetown Harbour.","wpu":"York Point, Prince Edward Island","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1a/York_Point_Road.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Queens Royalty, Prince Edward Island","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":46.264,"lo":-63.131,"d":3698,"ds":"Queens Royalty is the royalty for Queens County, Prince Edward Island, Canada. The township was established as part of the colonial survey of 1764 undertaken by Capt. Samuel J. Holland.","wpu":"Queens Royalty, Prince Edward Island","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bf/Map_of_Prince_Edward_Island_highlighting_Queens_Royalty.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Haszard Point Range Front","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":46.194361,"lo":-63.073667,"d":5674,"ds":"The Haszard Point Range Front is one of two range lights, the front light and the rear light, on Prince Edward Island, Canada. They were built in 1889, and are still active.","wpu":"Haszard Point Range Front","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Haszard_Point_Front_Range_Lighthouse_%2822101222268%29.jpg/960px-Haszard_Point_Front_Range_Lighthouse_%2822101222268%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Sherwood, Prince Edward Island","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":46.283333,"lo":-63.133333,"d":5854,"ds":"Sherwood is a neighbourhood of the city of Charlottetown in central Queens County, Prince Edward Island, Canada. Sherwood is centrally located in Charlottetown on the border of Queens Royalty and the township of Lot 33.","wpu":"Sherwood, Prince Edward Island","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Charlottetown%2C_Prince_Edward_Island_Location.png/960px-Charlottetown%2C_Prince_Edward_Island_Location.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Cornwall, Prince Edward Island","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":46.24065,"lo":-63.200911,"d":5936,"ds":"Cornwall is a Canadian town located in Queens County, Prince Edward Island. The town is located immediately west of the provincial capital Charlottetown.","wpu":"Cornwall, Prince Edward Island","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Cornwall%2C_PEI.jpg/960px-Cornwall%2C_PEI.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Charlottetown meteorite","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":46.289083,"lo":-63.068517,"d":7782,"ds":"The Charlottetown meteorite was a meteorite fall observed on July 25, 2024. It is notable as the first meteorite known with video and audio of the impact recorded and as the only known meteorite fall in Prince Edward Island, Canada. The Charlottetown meteorite is classified as H5 ordinary chondrite.","wpu":"Charlottetown meteorite","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Charlottetown_meteorite_impact_splotch.jpg/960px-Charlottetown_meteorite_impact_splotch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Lot 32, Prince Edward Island","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":46.266667,"lo":-63.233333,"d":9226,"ds":"Lot 32 is a township in Queens County, Prince Edward Island, Canada. It is part of Charlotte Parish. Lot 32 was awarded to Sir William Young, 1st Baronet in the 1767 land lottery.","wpu":"Lot 32, Prince Edward Island","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/27/Map_of_Prince_Edward_Island_highlighting_Lot_32.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"}],"about":{"ds":"Charlottetown is the capital and largest city of the Canadian province of Prince Edward Island, and the county seat of Queens County. Named after Queen Charlotte, Charlottetown was an unincorporated town until it was incorporated as a city in 1855. It was the site of the famous Charlottetown Conference in 1864, the first gathering of Canadian and Maritime statesmen to discuss the proposed Maritime Union.","wpu":"Charlottetown","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Charlottetown%2C_PEI_skyline.jpg/960px-Charlottetown%2C_PEI_skyline.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}